desc:GFX G Judgement [Arcana synth]
//tags: instrument synth analogue polyphonic brass polysynth embouchure pitch envelope ladder filter unison flanger chorus drive tape delay arcana
//author: JGWizrad / Garden FX (GFX)
//
// Requires gfx-drift, gfx-output, gfx-ui, gfx-panel, gfx-instrument, gfx-voice and gfx-clip (.jsfx-inc) in the same folder.
//
// JUDGEMENT (card XX of the GFX Arcana series): the trumpet call, the awakening, the whole section rising at once.
// A vintage analogue BRASS synthesizer in the manner of the late-70s modular and the big voice-card polysynths: eight
// voice cards, each a stack of oscillators into a warm resonant low-pass and a VCA, with the pitch-envelope
// "EMBOUCHURE" - every note's attack starts a set interval off its pitch and lips down onto it - and a section of
// players that are never quite alike.
//   OSCILLATORS  per voice: OSC 1 and OSC 2 (SAW or PULSE on two lit keys - the change crossfades - COARSE in
//              semitones, -24 .. +24; OSC 2 also FINE, +/- 50 cents; LEVEL each), PW (the pulses' width, both
//              oscillators), SUB (a square one or two octaves under OSC 1, drop-down, crossfaded; LEVEL) and BREATH
//              (noise through the filter, following the amp, with a puff at each attack while the embouchure lands).
//              All band-limited (PolyBLEP), so the top octave stays clean.
//   FILTER     a warm resonant low-pass: 24 dB (a four-pole ladder with a soft-saturating feedback loop) or 12 dB (a
//              two-pole state-variable, OTA-like), on two lit keys (crossfaded). CUTOFF (the black cap), RESO, ENV
//              (the filter envelope's depth, +/- 6 octaves), KEY (key tracking, 0 - 100 %, about middle C), VEL (the
//              key velocity to brightness: a soft note is darker and opens less).
//   ENVELOPES  a dual-role ADSR: the FILTER / AMP keys pick which envelope the four faders edit (ATTACK, DECAY,
//              SUSTAIN, RELEASE); both always run, side by side - the filter envelope into the cutoff (ENV), the amp
//              envelope into the VCA. LINK (lit): the hard-wired parallel routing - the FILTER envelope's one shape
//              drives both the cutoff and the VCA. VEL: the key velocity to the level (0 = every note the same).
//   EMBOUCHURE the pitch envelope: each note starts AMOUNT off its pitch (-12 .. +12 semitones, in cents: shown as
//              the interval - up to a major 2nd above is the classic brass blip, below is a lip-up, an octave an
//              effect) and glides onto it over TIME (2 ms - 1 s) on a CURVE (-100 % = it drops at once and settles
//              slowly, 0 = straight, +100 % = it holds and lands late). VEL: how much a soft note softens it.
//              Legato notes in UNISON are re-tongued at half the amount.
//   DETUNE     the big knob, top right: the beating and the micro-drift when the chord lands - OSC 2 pulls away
//              from OSC 1, each voice card sits a little sharp or flat of the next and wanders slowly, every note
//              lands with a small detune that settles over a third of a second, and a UNISON stack fans wider.
//   LFO        two LFOs: RATE (0.05 - 20 Hz) or SYNC (a division of the project tempo: 2 bars .. 1/32, locked to the
//              timeline while REAPER plays), SHAPE (sine, triangle, square (rounded), saw down, random), DELAY (each
//              note's LFO waits half the delay, then fades in over the other half). The MATRIX: a depth knob for each
//              LFO into PITCH (vibrato, cents), CUTOFF (growl, up to 3 octaves), PW (pulse width) and PAN (stereo
//              drift: each voice card wanders on its own phase). WHEEL: which LFO the mod wheel (CC1) brings in -
//              that LFO's depths are scaled by the wheel (OFF: the wheel does nothing).
//   VOICES     POLY (eight voices; a new note takes the same key's voice, else a free one, else the quietest
//              released, else the oldest - faded out in 4 ms first) or UNISON (one note at a time, last-note
//              priority, STACK 2 - 8 voices on it, fanned in pitch by DETUNE and across the stereo field by SPREAD).
//              GLIDE (portamento, 0 - 2 s); LEGATO lit: it glides only between joined notes, else always.
//              SPREAD: the voice cards across the stereo field. BEND: the pitch-bend range.
//   DRIVE      a solid-state transformer / preamp saturation (the house drive standard: an anti-aliased knee
//              clipper, a drive-tracking pre-filter, and the knee softening as it is pushed - a character stage),
//              slightly asymmetric: DRIVE, TONE, LEVEL. IN.
//   FLANGER    stereo (the right side a quarter-cycle on): RATE, DEPTH, FEEDBACK (+/-), MIX. IN.
//   CHORUS     a vintage analogue ensemble (three dark voices a side): RATE, DEPTH, MIX. IN.
//   DELAY      a warm tape-style echo: TIME (free, 20 ms - 1.5 s) or SYNC (a division), FEEDBACK, TONE (the repeats'
//              darkening), WOW (the tape's slow wow and fast flutter), DIFFUSE (each repeat blurred further; the first
//              stays clear), MIX. IN. The repeats saturate softly on the tape.
//              The chain: voices - DRIVE - FLANGER - CHORUS - DELAY - the output stage.
//   FATE       the series' drift (0 - 100 %, 50 % = the standard amount), here SECTION PLAYERS: every voice card
//              plays like a different player - its own embouchure depth, its own glide and lip time, its own
//              tuning - fixed to its slot, each slowly varying; and the whole instrument wanders a little.
//   VOLUME, LEVEL, SAT (the output soft clip is always on).
// MIDI: notes (velocity), sustain pedal (CC64), mod wheel (CC1), pitch bend, CC120 / CC123 all notes off; the channel
// drop-down in the title bar. A preset change (and a POLY / UNISON or STACK change) fades out, clears and fades in.

import gfx-drift.jsfx-inc
import gfx-output.jsfx-inc
import gfx-ui.jsfx-inc
import gfx-panel.jsfx-inc
import gfx-instrument.jsfx-inc
import gfx-voice.jsfx-inc
import gfx-clip.jsfx-inc

slider1:0<0,1,1{Saw,Pulse}>-Osc 1 wave
slider2:0<-24,24,1>-Osc 1 coarse (st)
slider3:50<5,95,1>-Pulse width (%)
slider4:80<0,100,1>-Osc 1 level (%)
slider5:0<0,1,1{Saw,Pulse}>-Osc 2 wave
slider6:0<-24,24,1>-Osc 2 coarse (st)
slider7:6<-50,50,0.1>-Osc 2 fine (cents)
slider8:70<0,100,1>-Osc 2 level (%)
slider9:0<0,1,1{1 octave down,2 octaves down}>-Sub octave
slider10:0<0,100,1>-Sub level (%)
slider11:6<0,100,1>-Breath (%)
slider12:900<20,20000,1>-Cutoff (Hz)
slider13:15<0,100,1>-Resonance (%)
slider14:55<-100,100,1>-Filter env amount (%)
slider15:50<0,100,1>-Key track (%)
slider16:1<0,1,1{12 dB,24 dB}>-Filter slope
slider17:40<0,100,1>-Velocity to brightness (%)
slider18:60<1,5000,1>-Filter attack (ms)
slider19:600<1,10000,1>-Filter decay (ms)
slider20:45<0,100,1>-Filter sustain (%)
slider21:300<1,10000,1>-Filter release (ms)
slider22:15<1,5000,1>-Amp attack (ms)
slider23:800<1,10000,1>-Amp decay (ms)
slider24:85<0,100,1>-Amp sustain (%)
slider25:220<1,10000,1>-Amp release (ms)
slider26:0<0,1,1{Off,Linked}>-Envelope link
slider27:50<0,100,1>-Velocity to level (%)
slider28:1<-12,12,0.01>-Embouchure amount (st)
slider29:60<2,1000,1>-Embouchure time (ms)
slider30:-40<-100,100,1>-Embouchure curve (%)
slider31:50<0,100,1>-Embouchure velocity (%)
slider32:35<0,100,1>-Detune (%)
slider33:5.2<0.05,20,0.01>-LFO I rate (Hz)
slider34:0<0,4,1{Sine,Triangle,Square,Saw down,Random}>-LFO I shape
slider35:0.6<0,5,0.01>-LFO I delay (s)
slider36:0<0,13,1{Free,2 bars,1 bar,1/2,1/2 T,1/4 D,1/4,1/4 T,1/8 D,1/8,1/8 T,1/16,1/16 T,1/32}>-LFO I sync
slider37:0.35<0.05,20,0.01>-LFO II rate (Hz)
slider38:1<0,4,1{Sine,Triangle,Square,Saw down,Random}>-LFO II shape
slider39:0<0,5,0.01>-LFO II delay (s)
slider40:0<0,13,1{Free,2 bars,1 bar,1/2,1/2 T,1/4 D,1/4,1/4 T,1/8 D,1/8,1/8 T,1/16,1/16 T,1/32}>-LFO II sync
slider41:12<0,100,0.1>-LFO I to pitch (cents)
slider42:0<0,100,1>-LFO I to cutoff (%)
slider43:0<0,100,1>-LFO I to pulse width (%)
slider44:0<0,100,1>-LFO I to pan (%)
